From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: name the board as Linux does

U-Boot's device tree calls the board "Radxa A7S". The board is the Radxa
Cubie A7S, and that is the model in Linux's device tree. With EFI the
SMBIOS tables take the system and baseboard product from this model, so
the OS reported "radxa Radxa A7S" while its own device tree said "Radxa
Cubie A7S"; the banner and BL31 print it too. Nothing matches on it.

The manufacturer stays the compatible's vendor prefix, "radxa", as U-Boot
derives it for every board without an SMBIOS node.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 30eec55d011..2f505f1df40 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 
 / {
-	model = "Radxa A7S";
+	model = "Radxa Cubie A7S";
 	compatible = "radxa,cubie-a7s", "allwinner,sun60i-a733";
 
 	aliases {
